{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,6} |P2′|delegat'\"' docs/design/yang.preludes.md docs/design/datom.world.md && rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g '*clojure*' -g 'core_module.cljc' -g '*analyze-deps*' | head -110\"","aggregated_output":"docs/design/datom.world.md:5:# DATOM.WORLD ARCHITECTURAL FOUNDATIONS & DEVELOPMENT RULES\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:7:## Core Philosophy\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:14:### Foundational Axioms\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:24:## Non-Negotiable Invariants\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:34:## Tuples and Datoms\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:42:## Streams\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:68:### Host Boundaries\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:73:## Architectural Commitments\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:80:## Design Principles\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:112:## Code Style\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:120:## Development Workflow\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:132:### Problem Decomposition\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:141:## Operational & Specialized Guides\ndocs/design/datom.world.md:146:- **Agent Delegation**: See [`docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md`](../agents/roles/orchestrator.md) for collaboration protocols and delegating tasks or reviews through `agy`, `cmd`, `glm`, `deepseek`, and `codex`; each orchestrator session has its own append-only log at `orchestrator-logs/<unix-time-stamp>-<brief-orchestrator-descriptive-name>.md` under the repository root.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:5:# yang.preludes: configurable and composable preludes for Yang frontends\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:15:- **2026-11-21 (r7 → r8 reconciliation):** Addressed all findings from the r7 architect review (thread `01a1faa3-bb7e-7c30-b3bf-cedbad008bfc`; 8 HIGH, 1 MEDIUM, plus default-profile regressions): (H1) explicit default-selector mechanism — the composition's immutable configuration carries the preferred `[id revision]`, applied at the normal request entry, with two-revision / legacy-pin / in-flight-snapshot gates; (H2) per-frontend **entry-lowering contracts** emitting the landed native entry shapes (`py` 1-arg `run-main`, `js` 1-operand, `php` 2-or-4 with request stream) alongside the Clojure resolver-bearing 2-arg shape; (H3) ONE derivation record (frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor, resolved runtime closure, input, output), pins reconciled by module symbol before lowering, dependency-first installation in linked composition, resolver derivation in provenance / live cell in the task; (H4) complete effect-unwind traversal per frame kind with exactly-once cleanup, a P2′ cold-error policy for plain `yang.clojure`, `clojure.core.impl` owning zero cells while declaring its runtime effects; (H5) address-bound export-**role** evidence (same-arity wrong-role fails closed); (H6) the §5.1 example labeled a Track B recipe recording bundled shape, linked trailing forms, pins, and C1 behavior independently; (H7) slice repair — P1′ clj-only synthetic fixtures, P2′ native collection invocation + bundled shadowing, P3′ the real cross-syntax unwind; (H8) boxed conversion/true-division at the host boundary, zero-raw-double scoped to boxed-path profiles; (M9) `yang.core.defquoted` naming consistency, r6 gates attached verbatim to Track B, oracle assignment (legacy pins ← native oracles, default ← capability refusals); (R) default-profile regressions — unqualified `:k` admission, cross-carrier integer identity, `:clj/unbound` distinguishability, canonical order settled to Jing encoded-byte order.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:24:## 1. Problem statement and repository baseline\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:26:### 1.1 Current repository baseline\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:48:### 1.2 Three problems to solve together\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:50:1. **Host representation leaks in guest UAST:** Bare VM primitives (`+`, `-`, `=`, `get`, `assoc`, `vec`, `kind/str`) delegate directly to host values, leaking JVM vs. Node/CLJS vs. Dart/CLJD vs. Jolt differences (`Float64` boxing, `BigInt` mixing, `NaN`/`-0.0` equality, CLJS joined-keyword collapse `(keyword nil \"a/b\") == (keyword \"a\" \"b\")`, HAMT map/set iteration order, float formatting). Patching around those leaks in guest UAST produces hundreds of lines of slow, fragile code (`admit-key!`, $O(n \\log n)$ `canonical-compare`, raw-double leaf-frame rules).\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:56:## 2. Derivation from foundations and non-negotiable invariants\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:60:### 2.1 Foundational axioms & three-tier hybrid rationale\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:74:### 2.1a Alignment with the tao architecture's second axiom (`yang.tao.md` §2.2)\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:84:### 2.2 Non-negotiable invariants\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:103:## 3. Three-tier hybrid architecture & prelude layering\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:134:### 3.1 Litmus test: Native Host `:pure` vs. Guest `%capture` Effects vs. VM Effects\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:142:### 3.2 Explicit exclusions from Layer 2a (`yrt.*`)\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:156:## 4. Host `:pure` core extensions & Layer 2a (`yrt.*`) specifications\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:158:### 4.1 Native host `:pure` core extensions (`data`, `float`, `kind`)\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:185:### 4.2 `yang.call` *(existing Layer-2a leaf)*\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:189:### 4.3 `yrt.effect` — Unified guest algebraic effects over `%capture`\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:231:### 4.4 `yrt.int` — Exact-integer adapters and radix scanners\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:242:### 4.5 `yrt.safepoint` *(Track B — deferred)*\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:248:## 5. Declarative prelude composition, recipes, and admission\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:252:### 5.1 Emission recipe vs. resolved runtime profile\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:301:### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:314:## 6. Preludes as swappable libraries: the semantics descriptor contract\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:316:### 6.1 Focused profile scope: Yin/Clojure DEFAULT + Native legacy track\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:325:### 6.2 Core vs. Frontend ownership boundary\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:336:### 6.3 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:468:### 6.4 Validation, lexical hygiene, authority checks, and parameterization\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:483:### 6.5 Frontend SPI and provenance integration (`yang.frontend`)\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:493:## 7. Case study: `yang.python` with a `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:495:### 7.1 Value representation & semantic mapping\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:514:### 7.2 Portable numeric & collection contract (`clj.py` over `:pure` host core + `yrt.effect`)\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:528:   - `+`, `-`, `*`, unary `-`, unary `+`, `/`, `//`, `%`, `**`, and `<`/`<=`/`>`/`>=` delegate directly to boxed `yin.vm.float` exports (`float/add`, `float/sub`, `float/mul`, `float/neg`, `float/div-checked`, `float/floordiv-mod`, `float/fpow-half`, `float/neg-pow`, `float/compare`) and `integer/compare-float` (via boxed float helper).\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:532:   - **Equality:** `clj.py/eq` delegates directly to **`data/equiv`**; `clj.py/ne` delegates to `(not (data/equiv a b))`.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:533:   - **Deterministic traversal:** Map/set iteration delegates directly to **`data/canonical-entries`**.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:535:### 7.3 Python lowering Hook ABI & `clj.py` adapters\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:542:| `:fn/make` | `[fname spec defaults kwdefaults code]` | Accepts the 5 arguments from `yang.python.antlr.lower/function-value:1870`; delegates to trusted Layer-2b **`clj/make-callable`** (`§7.4`). |\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:546:| `:ctrl/raise` | `[e]` | Calls `clj/raise` (delegating to `yrt.effect/raise` on `(clj/rt-ctx)`). |\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:554:### 7.4 Unified trusted `clj` callable bridge, cross-unit admission, and §8.10.7 validation\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:569:### 7.5 Two-module portable `clojure.core` contract (`clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core`)\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:574:   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; **zero state cells**). Its guest **policy tags** (`:coll/unsupported-key`, `:math/*`, `:int/*`) live in the handler contract installed by the owning entry (`clj.py/run-main` at P3′, plain `yang.clojure`'s own cold-error policy at P2′) — they are NOT part of the linker-derived VM effect footprint; only the underlying **VM effects** its definitions perform are declared through the existing linker footprint mechanism (`yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:578:     - `impl-inc`, `impl-dec`, `impl-rem`, `impl-int?`: delegate to `integer/*` + `yrt.int/check-limit` and `float/add`/`float/sub`.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:579:     - `impl-not=`: delegates to `(not (data/equiv a b))`.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:580:     - `impl-str`: deterministic renderer delegating ints to `integer/format`, floats to `float/format`, keywords/symbols to `kind/namespace` + `kind/name`, maps/sets to `data/canonical-entries`, and authenticated cells to `\"#<fn>\"`.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:589:### 7.6 Concrete lowering example\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:607:## 8. Portability, content addressing, and malleability\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:609:### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:616:### 8.2 Dependency graph and malleability (`docs/agents/malleability.md`)\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:634:### 8.3 Content-addressing and golden discipline (Clean-Slate)\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:640:## 9. Phased implementation roadmap and acceptance gates\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:647:| **P1′ — `yrt.effect` + `yrt.int` with Clojure-only consumers; unified trusted `clj`** | Implement stateless `yrt.effect` (5-slot `data/nth` frames, abortive `raise`/`try-value`/`try-orelse`/`try-finally`/`call-ec`, plus resumable `handle`/`perform` — the frame design anticipates py/php `:depth` accounting but only clj/clj.py exercise it) and `yrt.int`; upgrade `clj` to the unified trusted form (two-step `make-callable`, evaluated `assoc` conditions, `invoke-callable`, `prim-get`/`prim-assoc`, retiring `yang.clojure`'s `dsg__call_token` / inline provenance ops); add `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` for bundled `clj`. **py/js/php preludes untouched** — they keep their own mechanisms. | Refresh `clj`/`yang.clojure` goldens cleanly; py/js/php goldens untouched | `yrt.effect` unit tests (abortive, `finally`, resumable one-shot `handle`/`perform`, cold policy traps) across semantic/stack/register VMs; bundled/linked `yang.clojure` parity under shadowed `(defn get ...)`; clj-only synthetic nonzero depth/base fixtures exercising the `:depth` slot; independent concurrent `clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. (H7 repair: native collection invocation — including the landed fixture where a locally bound map invoked with `:k` returns 9, which requires the native data-call dispatch to admit locally bound maps — and bundled primitive shadowing through the new standard library gate in the P2′ row below; the REAL cross-syntax `clj → clj.py → clj` unwind with cleanup and context restoration gates SOLELY in the P3′ row.) |\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:648:| **P2′ — Unified `clojure.core` + `yang.clojure` migration** | Publish collision-free `clojure.core.impl` (pure, `impl-*` prefix, `admit-key?`-guarded) + cell-free `clojure.core` facade; migrate `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core`. | Refresh `yang.clojure` goldens cleanly | Native collection invocation through the new standard library (the locally-bound-map `:k` → 9 fixture) and bundled primitive shadowing of bare `get`/`assoc` (which otherwise resolve through the source store before VM primitives); unified `yang.clojure` suite green. The real `clj → clj.py → clj` cross-syntax unwind (cleanup + context restoration) gates ONLY at P3′, after `clj.py` exists. |\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:655:## 10. Owner decisions and disposition ledger\nAGENTS.md\ncollab/general/tiers-runs/yang.clojure.stream-eval-test.slow.log\ncollab/general/tiers-runs/yang.clojure.stream-eval-test.quick.log\nbin/analyze-deps.clj\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\ntest/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc\ntest/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\ntest/yang/clojure_test.clj\norchestrator-logs/1794314498-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-seat-takeover.md\norchestrator-logs/1793187400000-glm-yang-clojure-hardening.md\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md\norchestrator-logs/1793385006-zcode-glm-5.3-flash-yang-clojure-track.md\norchestrator-logs/1793188658-yang-clojure-hardening-claude.md\norchestrator-logs/1793947104-agy-gemini-3.8-flash-yang-clojure-seat-takeover.md\npublic/chp/blog/daostar-vs-datastar-vs-electric-clojure.blog\npublic/chp/blog/why-clojure-has-no-linker.blog\ncollab/exception-track/1794343003000-to-yangclojure-r3-inflight-r4-scope-confirmed.md\ncollab/exception-track/1794407000000-to-yangclojure-landing-sequence-accepted-cc3-proceeds.md\ncollab/exception-track/1795050000000-yangclojure-r3-ready-kit-gap-flagged.md\ncollab/exception-track/1794558000000-to-yangclojure-correction-finally-lift-contested.md\ncollab/exception-track/1794598000000-blog-tco-why-clojure-has-it.prompt.md\ncollab/exception-track/1794401000000-to-yangclojure-port-trigger-active-scopes.md\ncollab/exception-track/1795500000000-yangclojure-stood-down-from-r3.md\ncollab/exception-track/1794970000000-to-yangclojure-your-r3-then-r4.md\ncollab/exception-track/1794341300000-reviewer-r3-exception-cloju