s role owns no permanent file list. Each task defines the artifacts it may\ninspect or change and any permitted expansion.\n\n## Core Responsibilities\n\n1. **Syntax Independence**: Maintain the core principle that syntax is merely a superficial projection of underlying Universal AST datoms.\n2. **Deterministic Lowering**: Ensure that source code lowers unambiguously to structured datoms with canonical content hashes.\n3. **Multi-Target Interoperability**: Support lowering from Clojure, Python, and other dialects into the shared Yin.VM instruction set.\n4. **Macro Hygiene & Stigmergy**: Implement macro transformation pipelines that preserve source location metadata and lexically scoped bindings.\n\n## Implementation Prompt Template\n\n```text\nCreated-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCreated-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\n# Task: <Task Name>\n\nRole: Yang Compiler and Universal AST Engineer\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: <model-name> | Assigned: <local timestamp> | Status: active | Rationale: <why>\n\nImplement <task> in <repository-root>. Read <governing-design-file>,\n<source-files>, and <test-files> first. Acceptance criteria:\n- <criterion-1>\n- <criterion-2>\n- <criterion-3>\n\nWork only in named files. If a required dependency demands expansion, stop and\nrequest authorization before editing it. Preserve unrelated changes, do not\nweaken tests, and preserve syntax independence and deterministic lowering. Run\nfocused tests and lint, and inspect the final diff.\n\nBegin the final response exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n\nReport changed files, exact test/check outcomes, unresolved concerns, and any\nincomplete work. Do not claim edits or tests that did not occur.\n```\n18:bb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\n46:# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n48:# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n50:# (`clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>`, Node `--test=<ns>`, Dart `--only <ns>`) --\n79:                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\n108:bb test:quick-sharded --changed src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\n110:bb test:quick-sharded --list --changed src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\n130:`clojure -M:test -e :slow -n <ns> ...` process, with at most N JVMs running.\n162:| Foundation code owned by a layer-0 entry in `subsystems.edn`, or `yang.clojure`, `yang.php`, | `bb test:quick-sharded --changed <paths>` — broad selected JVM        |\n234:Laptop pilot (2026-10-29, 8 cores, 4 workers, `yang.clojure.cljc` changed):\n275:1. **G0 Iterate**: Run only the subsystem's JVM lane (`bb test:sub:clj <own>` or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`).\n278:   failing test, never the whole suite.** JVM: `clojure -M:test -n <ns>` (a single\n329:  `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.dht-process-test`, after\n344:clj -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n358:script compiles every test namespace via `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n362:under `test/`, so plain `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd test` still works. Tests of\n378:  `clojure -M:test -e :slow` on the JVM; the Node and Dart lanes skip the\n381:  `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>` on the JVM.\n429:NS=<namespace> clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:t {:extra-paths [\"test\"]}}}' -M:t timing.clj\n431:#   (binding [clojure.test/*test-out* (java.io.StringWriter.)] (clojure.test/test-vars [v]))\n471:  t0=$(date +%s); clojure -M:test -e :slow \"${args[@]}\" >\"$OUT/$s.log\" 2>&1; rc=$?\n493:  clojure -M:test -i :slow -n \"$n\" > \"$OUT/$n.log\" 2>&1; rc=$?\n510:| `shiva.stigmergy.systems` | 24 / 62 GB | Server snapshot: java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.1. The repo's `mise.toml` selects Flutter `latest` on beta, not a fixed version. Activate the repo toolchain before running any lane. |\n511:| `jupiter.stigmergy.systems` | 48 / 62 GB | Server snapshot (rechecked 2026-10-29): java 21, clojure 1.12.4