{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '268,370p;437,495p;525,553p;756,788p;1033,1057p;1978,2014p' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc; sed -n '410,460p' src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc; sed -n '398,474p' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(defn literal?\n  \"Check if a value is a literal (self-evaluating).\"\n  [form]\n  (or (number? form)\n      (string? form)\n      (true? form)\n      (false? form)\n      (nil? form)\n      (keyword? form)\n      (vector? form)\n      (set? form)\n      (map? form)))\n\n\n(defn constant-form?\n  \"True when compiling `form` yields a fixed value independent of the\n   environment: scalars, quoted forms, and collections built entirely from\n   constants. A symbol is never constant (it is a variable reference). A\n   `quote` counts as constant only at the top level: nested inside a\n   collection it must reach compile-form so the quote is stripped and the\n   inner form evaluated as data.\"\n  ([form] (constant-form? form true))\n  ([form top-level?]\n   (cond\n     (or (nil? form) (number? form) (string? form)\n         (true? form) (false? form) (keyword? form)) true\n     (and (seq? form) (empty? form)) true\n     (seq? form) (and top-level? (= 2 (count form)) (= 'quote (first form)))\n     (or (vector? form) (set? form)) (every? #(constant-form? % false) form)\n     (map? form) (and (every? #(constant-form? % false) (keys form))\n                      (every? #(constant-form? % false) (vals form)))\n     :else false)))\n\n\n(defn- content-root\n  \"The canonical semantic-bytecode root of one compiled child: the content\n   address of its projected executable content. Constructed collections\n   order their operands by these addresses (constructed-collections-v1);\n   the projection here is temporary compile-time data, never a published\n   root or ordering table.\"\n  [ast]\n  (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))\n\n\n(defn- compile-constructed-collection\n  \"Lower a collection literal with dynamic elements to constructor calls over\n   existing portable primitives, so unquoted vectors/maps/sets evaluate their\n   elements like Clojure. Constant collections stay :literal nodes.\n\n   [e1 e2 ...]  => (conj [] e1 e2 ...)\n   #{e1 e2 ...} => (conj #{} e1 e2 ...)\n   {k1 v1 ...}  => (assoc {} k1 v1 k2 v2 ...)\n\n   A host map or set has no portable iteration order, so a map's pairs and\n   a set's elements enter the operand vector in compiled-content order\n   (constructed-collections-v1): each child compiles once, pairs sort\n   ascending by jing/canonical-compare over the two-element vector\n   [key-root value-root] of the children's projected roots (key-root\n   primary, value-root secondary), set elements by their own root, after\n   the unchanged seed operand and before the unchanged operator resolution\n   and tail mark. Equal sort keys are equal executable content under the\n   content-address integrity contract, so a tie keeps its occurrences and\n   needs no further tie-break; no child is recompiled, deduplicated or\n   evaluated, and each compiled AST keeps its own attached metadata. A\n   vector retains its written element order.\"\n  [form tail? env macro-env]\n  (let [ctor (cond\n               (vector? form) ['conj []]\n               (set? form) ['conj #{}]\n               :else ['assoc {}])\n        [op seed] ctor\n        compile-child #(compile-form % false env macro-env)\n        ;; each pair/element keeps its compiled ASTs and their content keys\n        ;; together, so sorting never recompiles or loses an occurrence\n        sorted-children\n        (cond\n          (vector? form) {:order :written, :children (mapv compile-child form)}\n          (map? form)\n          {:order :canonical\n           :records (mapv (fn [k v]\n                            (let [ck (compile-child k)\n                                  cv (compile-child v)]\n                              {:sort-key [(content-root ck) (content-root cv)]\n                               :children [ck cv]}))\n                          (keys form) (vals form))}\n          :else\n          {:order :canonical\n           :records (mapv (fn [e]\n                            (let [ce (compile-child e)]\n                              {:sort-key [(content-root ce)]\n                               :children [ce]}))\n                          form)})\n        operands (case (:order sorted-children)\n                   :written (:children sorted-children)\n                   (into [] (mapcat :children)\n                         (sort-by :sort-key jing/canonical-compare\n                                  (:records sorted-children))))\n        call {:type :application,\n              :operator {:type :variable, :name op},\n              :operands (into [{:type :literal, :value seed}] operands)}]\n    (cond-> call tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n\n\n(def ^:private helper-names\n  (set (map symbol [\"first\" \"rest\" \"empty?\"])))\n\n\n(defn- locals\n  [env]\n  (::locals env #{}))\n\n\n(defn- with-locals\n  [env names]\n  (when-let [hit (and (::convention env) (some #{'conj 'vec} names))]\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"Binding \" hit \" would capture the argument-vector constructor\")\n                    {:names names})))\n  (when (and (::invoker env) (some #{'invoke-value} names))\n    (throw (ex-info \"Binding invoke-value would capture the guest collection invoker\" {:names names})))\n  (assoc env ::locals (into (locals env) (remove #(= '& %)) names)))\n\n\n(def ^:private reserved-prefix \"dsg__\")\n\n\n(defn- reject!\n  [message data]\n  (throw (ex-info message data)))\n\n\n(defn- reserved-name?\n  [sym]\n  (= reserved-prefix (subs (name sym) 0 (min (count (name sym))\n                                             (count reserved-prefix)))))\n\n\n(defn- check-def-name!\n  \"A definition name is a plain symbol outside the reserved prefix.\"\n  [operator sym]\n  (when-not (and (symbol? sym) (nil? (namespace sym)))\n    (reject! (str operator \" needs a plain symbol name\") {:name sym}))\n  (when (reserved-name? sym)\n    (reject! \"Definition name uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n             {:name sym, :prefix reserved-prefix})))\n\n\n(defn- check-binder!\n  \"A binder is a plain symbol or a nested sequential pattern; anything else\n   (maps, keywords, literals) is outside the supported surface.\"\n  [b pattern]\n  (cond\n    (and (symbol? b) (nil? (namespace b)) (not= '& b))\n    (when (reserved-name? b)\n      (reject! \"Binding name uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n               {:binder b, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n    (vector? b) nil\n    (map? b) (reject! \"Map destructuring is not supported\"\n                      {:binder b, :pattern pattern})\n    :else (reject! \"Unsupported binding form\" {:binder b, :pattern pattern})))\n\n\n(defn- parse-sequential-pattern\n              (recur (next xs) (conj positional x) rest-binder as-sym)))))))\n\n\n(defn- first-form\n  [cursor meta-map]\n  (cond-> (list 'first cursor)\n    meta-map (with-meta meta-map)))\n\n\n(defn- rest-form\n  [cursor meta-map env]\n  ;; Parameter and loop destructuring can be emitted after outcome lowering.\n  ;; Keep their cursors raw vectors even when the guest library defines rest\n  ;; with the argument-vector/outcome convention.\n  (cond-> (if (contains? (::defined env) 'rest)\n            (list 'data/subvec (list 'vec cursor) (list 'if (list 'empty? cursor) 0 1))\n            (list 'rest cursor))\n    meta-map (with-meta meta-map)))\n\n\n(defn- nthnext-form\n  \"Clojure's nthnext at a cursor: nil once exhausted, else the remainder.\"\n  [cursor meta-map]\n  (cond-> (list 'if (list 'empty? cursor) nil cursor)\n    meta-map (with-meta meta-map)))\n\n\n(defn- temp-symbol\n  [path meta-map]\n  [form]\n  (and (seq? form)\n       (symbol? (first form))\n       (contains? #{'fn 'if 'let 'quote 'do 'def 'dao.stream.apply/call 'defmacro 'loop 'recur} (first form))))\n\n\n(defn compile-literal\n  \"Compile a literal value to Universal AST.\"\n  [form _tail?]\n  {:type :literal, :value form})\n\n\n(defn compile-variable\n  \"Compile a variable reference (symbol) to Universal AST.\"\n  [sym _tail?]\n  {:type :variable, :name sym})\n\n\n(defn compile-def\n  \"Compile a def form to Universal AST.\n   Emits a yin/def application which requires environment support.\"\n  ([sym value env tail?] (compile-def sym value env tail? initial-macro-env))\n  ([sym value env tail? macro-env]\n   (check-def-name! 'def sym)\n   (cond-> {:type :application,\n            :operator {:type :variable, :name 'yin/def},\n            :operands [{:type :literal, :value sym}\n                       (compile-form value false env macro-env)]}\n     tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n\n\n(defn compile-lambda\n  \"Compile a lambda (fn) expression to Universal AST.\n\n(defn- source-meta\n  \"The source position keys of `form`'s reader metadata, or nil.\"\n  [form]\n  (not-empty (select-keys (meta form) source-keys)))\n\n\n(defn- arity-error-form\n  \"The raise of a call whose argument count no arity admits: it names the\n   function, never a zero-argument data/count refusal naming count. An\n   anonymous fn has no name: it is `:yin.k/kind :anonymous` and carries the\n   fn form's source position, when the reader gave one.\"\n  [fn-name source]\n  (list 'clj/throw\n        (cond-> {:yin.vm.data/reason :arity\n                 :yin.k/argc (list 'data/count av-sym)}\n          fn-name (assoc :yin.k/fn (list 'quote fn-name))\n          (nil? fn-name) (assoc :yin.k/kind :anonymous)\n          (and (nil? fn-name) source) (assoc :yin.k/source source))))\n\n\n(def outcome-adapter prelude/outcome-adapter)\n\n\n(defn- av-let\n(defn- check-program-symbols!\n  \"The program pre-pass. Quoted data is exempt. The reserved prefix names\n   compiler temporaries, so no user symbol may carry it in ANY position\n   (binder, reference, definition name); `loop` and `recur` are special forms,\n   so they may only head a list, never stand as a value or a binder.\"\n  [form]\n  (cond\n    (symbol? form)\n    (do (when (reserved-name? form)\n          (reject! \"Symbol uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n                   {:symbol form, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n        (when (and (nil? (namespace form)) (contains? #{'loop 'recur} form))\n          (reject! (str form \" is only legal in operator position\") {:symbol form})))\n    (seq? form)\n    (when-not (= 'quote (first form))\n      (let [head (first form)]\n        (when (and (symbol? head) (reserved-name? head))\n          (reject! \"Symbol uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n                   {:symbol head, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n        (when-not (symbol? head)\n          (check-program-symbols! head))\n        (run! check-program-symbols! (rest form))))\n    (map? form) (run! check-program-symbols! (concat (keys form) (vals form)))\n    (coll? form) (run! check-program-symbols! form)))\n\n\n(defn- lower-top-form\n  \"A non-definition top-level expression lowers like a function body (plain\n   values, `throw`/`try` onto the continuation family); definitions keep\n   their own lowering.\"\n  [env macro-env form]\n  (if (and (seq? form) (contains? #{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} (first form)))\n    form\n    (lower-function-body env macro-env [] [form])))\n\n\n(def ^:private local-call-runtime\n                :else (recur (inc i))))\n        (cond (< (count x) (count y)) -1\n              (> (count x) (count y)) 1\n              :else 0)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Kinds\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- data-number?\n  \"True when `x` is a host number or an exact-integer carrier, including\n   a JS or Dart big integer, which answers false to `number?`. A\n   closure, a continuation, nil and a map are not, whatever they answer\n   to `get`.\"\n  [x]\n  (or (number? x) (integer-host/big-carrier? x)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Floats: the seam between addressed float content and host arithmetic\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn float-value\n  \"The host double of number or float64 content `x`, for host arithmetic:\n   what the literal `1.0` is on each host, a double on the JVM and Dart, a\n   Number on JS. A prelude unwraps a float with this, computes on bare\n   numbers, and wraps the result back with `float64`.\"\n  [x]\n  (when-not (or (data-number? x) (cbor/float64? x))\n    (wrong-type! 'float-value 0 :number))\n  #?(:cljd (if (dart/is? x BigInt) (.toDouble ^BigInt x) (.toDouble ^num x))\n     :clj (double x)\n     :cljs (cond (number? x) x\n                 (cbor/float64? x) (.-v ^not-native x)\n                 :else (js/Number x))))\n\n\n(defn float64\n  \"Float content with the value of number `x`: Jing's float64, the form a\n   float keeps in any value that can reach an addressed row or image (a\n   double on the JVM and Dart, the float64 carrier on JS, where a bare\n   integral Number is an integer; dao.jing.cbor.md, Numeric identity). The\n   producer carries float kind; the codec never infers it.\"\n  [x]\n  (cbor/float64 (float-value x)))\n\n\n(defn- callable?\n  \"True when `x` can be applied: a host function, a closure or a\n   continuation. A map is never callable, whatever keys it carries.\"\n  (apply assoc coll (key/normalize k) v\n         (map-indexed (fn [i x] (if (even? i) (key/normalize x) x)) kvs)))\n\n(defn- normalize-map-conj [x]\n  (cond\n    (and (vector? x) (= 2 (count x))) [(key/normalize (nth x 0)) (nth x 1)]\n    (map? x) (into (empty x) (map (fn [[k v]] [(key/normalize k) v])) x)\n    (sequential? x) (map normalize-map-conj x)\n    :else x))\n\n(defn- collection-conj [coll & xs]\n  (apply conj coll\n         (map (fn [x]\n                (cond (set? coll) (key/normalize x)\n                      (map? coll) (normalize-map-conj x)\n                      :else x)) xs)))\n\n(defn- collection-get\n  ([coll k] (get coll (if (or (map? coll) (set? coll)) (key/normalize k) k)))\n  ([coll k default] (get coll (if (or (map? coll) (set? coll)) (key/normalize k) k) default)))\n\n\n(def primitives\n  \"The standard executable primitive registry, published with UCF §7.5.2\n   profiles. `:yin.k/function` is host-local; the five profile keys are the\n   portable publication. `:variadic` means the greatest listed fixed arity\n   extends to further arguments.\"\n  (let [pure (fn [name function arities]\n               [name (primitive-entry name function :pure arities #{})])]\n    (into {}\n          [(pure '+ + [0 1 2 :variadic])\n           (pure '- - [1 2 :variadic])\n           (pure '* * [0 1 2 :variadic])\n           (pure '/ checked-divide [1 2 :variadic])\n           (pure '= = [0 1 2 :variadic])\n           (pure '== = [0 1 2 :variadic])\n           (pure '!= not= [1 2 :variadic])\n           (pure '< < [1 2 :variadic])\n           (pure '> > [1 2 :variadic])\n           (pure '<= <= [1 2 :variadic])\n           (pure '>= >= [1 2 :variadic])\n           (pure 'not not [1])\n           (pure 'nil? nil? [1])\n           (pure 'empty? empty? [1])\n           (pure 'first first [1])\n           (pure 'rest (fn [a] (vec (rest a))) [1])\n           (pure 'conj collection-conj [1 2 :variadic])\n           (pure 'assoc collection-assoc [3 :variadic])\n           (pure 'get collection-get [2 3])\n           (pure 'vec vec [1])\n           ;; one arity: strict UTF-8 on every host (dao.host.text, slice\n           ;; H2, ratified OQ11: encoding arity 2 removed from portable profile)\n           (pure 'bytes->str\n                 (fn [b] (text/utf8-decode b))\n                 [1])\n           ['require (primitive-entry\n                       'require\n                       (fn [spec]\n                         (let [ns-sym (if (vector? spec) (first spec) spec)]\n                           (effect/make :module/require {:module ns-sym})))\n                       :effectful [1] #{:module/require})]\n           ['try-require (primitive-entry\n                           'try-require\n                           (fn [spec]\n                             (let [ns-sym (if (vector? spec) (first spec) spec)]\n                               (effect/make :module/try-require\n                                            {:module ns-sym})))\n                           :effectful [1] #{:module/try-require})]])))\n\n\n(def ^:private primitive-profile-keys\n  [:yin.k/profile :yin.k/class :yin.k/arities :yin.k/effects\n   :yin.k/host-state])\n\n\n(def primitive-profiles\n  \"Portable projection of the standard registry, retained as a convenience.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
