{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1057,1095p;1435,1489p' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc; sed -n '1,69p' src/cljc/yang/core/prelude_admission.cljc; sed -n '59,106p' test/yang/cc4_corpus.clj\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- av-let\n  \"(let [p0 (data/nth av 0) ...] body): positional parameters of one arity.\n   A body that recurs is a loop over the same bindings: one recur target per\n   arity. Under the outcome model the body is lowered first.\"\n  [env macro-env params body-forms]\n  (let [bindings (into [] (mapcat (fn [i p] [p (list 'data/nth av-sym i)]) (range) params))\n        lowered? (outcomes? env)\n        body (if lowered?\n               (lower-function-body env macro-env params body-forms)\n               (body-expression body-forms))]\n    (if (some mentions-recur? body-forms)\n      (with-meta (if lowered?\n                   (list 'loop bindings body)\n                   (list* 'loop bindings body-forms))\n        {::fn-loop true})\n      (list 'let bindings body))))\n\n\n(defn- av-dispatch\n  \"Nested ifs over the argument vector's count, one branch per arity\n   {:n count :form branch}. An unmatched count falls through to a\n   zero-argument data/count, which the data module refuses with :reason\n   :arity; under the outcome model it is an arity error outcome naming\n   `fn-name` (or the anonymous fn's `source`) instead.\"\n  [env fn-name source arities]\n  (let [counts (map :n arities)]\n    (when (not= (count counts) (count (set counts)))\n      (reject! \"Two arities with the same parameter count\" {:counts (vec counts)}))\n    (reduce (fn [else {:keys [n form]}]\n              (list 'if\n                    (list 'data/content= (list 'data/count av-sym) n)\n                    form\n                    else))\n            (if (outcomes? env) (arity-error-form fn-name source) (list 'data/count))\n            (reverse arities))))\n\n\n(defn- check-av-params!\n  [params]\n\n  Clojure: (if test consequent alternate)\n  AST: {:type :if\n        :test <compiled-test>\n        :consequent <compiled-consequent>\n        :alternate <compiled-alternate>}\n\n  An explicit `false` alternate is a value, not an absence: `alternate-present?`\n  distinguishes (if t c) from (if t c false).\"\n  ([test consequent alternate env tail?]\n   (compile-if test consequent alternate true env tail? initial-macro-env))\n  ([test consequent alternate alt-present? env tail?]\n   (compile-if test consequent alternate alt-present? env tail? initial-macro-env))\n  ([test consequent alternate alt-present? env tail? macro-env]\n   (cond-> {:type :if,\n            :test (compile-form test false env macro-env),\n            :consequent (compile-form consequent tail? env macro-env),\n            :alternate (if alt-present?\n                         (compile-form alternate tail? env macro-env)\n                         (compile-literal nil tail?))}\n     tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n\n\n(declare compile-let-simple)\n\n\n(defn compile-let\n  \"Compile a let binding to Universal AST.\n\n  Transforms let into nested lambda applications:\n  (let [x 1 y 2] (+ x y))\n  =>\n  ((fn [x] ((fn [y] (+ x y)) 2)) 1)\"\n  ([bindings body env tail?] (compile-let bindings body env tail? initial-macro-env))\n  ([bindings body env tail? macro-env]\n   (compile-let-simple (expand-bindings bindings env) body env tail? macro-env)))\n\n\n(defn- compile-let-simple\n  \"compile-let over a binding vector whose targets are all plain symbols.\"\n  [bindings body env tail? macro-env]\n  (if (empty? bindings)\n    ;; a function body is compiled in the scope the bindings built\n    (if (fn? body)\n      (body tail? env macro-env)\n      (compile-form body tail? env macro-env))\n    (let [[binding-name binding-value & rest-bindings] bindings\n          compiled-value (compile-form binding-value false env macro-env)\n          new-macro-env (shadow-macro-env macro-env [binding-name])\n          compiled-body (compile-let-simple rest-bindings body\n                                            (with-locals env [binding-name])\n                                            tail? new-macro-env)]\n      (cond-> {:type :application,\n               :operator\n               {:type :lambda, :params [binding-name], :body compiled-body},\n(ns yang.core.prelude-admission\n  \"Constructs declarations/specifications and checks registries; does not publish, link, or execute.\"\n  (:require [clojure.set :as set]\n            [clojure.string :as string]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(defn- refusal\n  [refusal-ns kind data]\n  (merge {(keyword refusal-ns \"refusal\") (keyword refusal-ns kind)} data))\n\n\n(defn host-declaration\n  \"`[n declaration]` for free name `n`: a primitive by its `vm/primitives`\n   profile, a host export `ns/name` by the profile address the registry's\n   host module `ns` publishes and its `:callable-effects` effect set; nil\n   when neither supplies it.\"\n  [registry n]\n  (if-let [profile (vm/profile-of vm/primitives n)]\n    [n profile]\n    (when-let [address (module/host-export-profile registry n)]\n      (let [entry (module/module-entry (:modules registry) (symbol (namespace n)))\n            f (get-in entry [:slice (symbol (name n))])]\n        [n {:yin.k/profile address,\n            :yin.k/effects (get (:callable-effects registry) f #{})}]))))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for module `module-name`.\n   `skip?` (n -> bool) marks free names a requirement already declares;\n   `requires` is the requirement map. A free name nothing supplies is\n   refused with `message` under `refusal-ns` before anything is published.\n   This namespace emits; it never publishes.\"\n  [{:keys [module-name ast exports requires free-names skip? registry message\n           refusal-ns]}]\n  {:name module-name,\n   :ast ast,\n   :exports exports,\n   :requires requires,\n   :primitives\n   (into {}\n         (keep (fn [n]\n                 (when-not (and skip? (skip? n))\n                   (or (host-declaration registry n)\n                       (throw (ex-info message\n                                       (refusal refusal-ns \"undeclared-free\"\n                                                {:name n})))))))\n         free-names)})\n\n\n(defn admit\n  \"Return `registry` when it supplies every one of `host-names`, else refuse\n   it before any program runs, naming each missing export in\n   `:<refusal-ns>/missing`.\"\n  [registry host-names message refusal-ns]\n  (let [missing (vec (sort-by str\n                              (remove #(some? (module/resolve-module\n                                                registry\n                                                (symbol (str (namespace %)\n                                                             \".\"\n                                                             (name %)))))\n                                      host-names)))]\n    (when (seq missing)\n      (throw (ex-info message\n                      (refusal refusal-ns \"host-names\"\n                               {(keyword refusal-ns \"missing\") missing}))))\n    registry))\n\n                                      ast)))\n         forms (quote [(defn replay\n                         [x]\n                         (let [[a b] [x 1.5]]\n                           (+ (identity ^:replay a)\n                              (identity ^:replay a) b)))\n                       (replay 2)])\n         projected (fn [id ast token]\n                     (let [ast (prepare ast)\n                           p (encoder/project\n                               (encoder/source-envelope :cc4/replay token [ast]))]\n                       {:id id :compiled ast\n                        :tree (first (:yin/batch p))\n                        :rows (:yin/frontend-metadata p)}))\n         ast (yang/compile-program forms)\n         macro-ast (yang/compile-program\n                     (quote [(defmacro twin\n                               [x]\n                               (yin/if (yin/literal true) x\n                                       (yin/application\n                                         (yin/variable (quote f))\n                                         [(yin/literal 1)])))\n                             (defn f\n                               [x]\n                               x)\n                             (twin (f 1))]))\n         expansion (:result (expand-like-the-repl (prepare macro-ast)))\n         store (mem/create-content-mem)\n         call-spec (update (call/module-spec publish-registry) :ast prepare)\n         call-result (publish/publish-module! store call-spec)\n         effect-result (publish/publish-module! store (effect/module-spec publish-registry))\n         clj-spec (update (clj-prelude/module-spec\n                            publish-registry (:address call-result)\n                            (:address effect-result))\n                          :ast prepare)\n         clj-result (publish/publish-module! store clj-spec)\n         published (fn [id result spec]\n                     (let [table (publish/published-call-site-table store result)]\n                       {:id id :compiled (:ast spec)\n                        :tree (or (:tree table)\n                                  (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (:ast spec)))\n                        :rows (or (:rows table) [])\n                        :addresses (assoc (dissoc (:call-sites result) :origin)\n                                          :manifest (:address result))\n                        :published-payloads\n                        (when (:call-sites result)\n                          (mapv #(jing/get store % nil)\n                                (map (:call-sites result)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
